{"_id":"68a736178ec3d8323af16440","nodeId":"BvV8VCX39wRB-g8WvGF1g","roadmapSlug":"docker","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:03.460Z","description":"# What are Namespaces?\n\nDocker namespaces are a Linux kernel feature that creates isolated environments for containers by providing separate instances of global system resources. Docker uses PID, NET, MNT, UTS, IPC, and USER namespaces to ensure each container believes it has its own unique resources, enabling lightweight, portable, and secure containerization.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Docker Namespaces","url":"https://docs.docker.com/engine/security/userns-remap/","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dbad9"},{"type":"article","title":"Linux Namespaces","url":"https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/namespaces.7.html","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dbada"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-30T07:56:48.897Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416d80","title":"DataCamp - Introduction to Docker","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/zzDy1W"},{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416df4","title":"DataCamp - Containerization and Virtualization","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/GbEdZ2"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/docker/content/BvV8VCX39wRB-g8WvGF1g.md"}